# W3-D (2026-10-03) — semgrep ignore file for the FayaNMS repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   The semgrep 1.179.0 upgrade (PR #56) surfaced exactly one finding that is
#   NOT resolvable by either a code fix or an inline `# nosemgrep:`
#   annotation:
#
#     generic.secrets.security.detected-private-key.detected-private-key
#     → mini-services/worker/harness/tls/sfos-webapi-key.pem
#
#   The file is the SFOS protocol-harness persona's self-signed loopback TLS
#   key (F-045 decision: banner-labeled demo personas are NOT secrets). It
#   CANNOT carry an inline annotation: any text before the
#   BEGIN-key marker line (or appended to it) makes
#   OpenSSL reject the key ("NO_START LINE" — verified with
#   crypto.createPrivateKey), and a trailing comment after the END line does
#   not cover the finding's line range for semgrep.
#
#   This is the same fixture already machine-triaged for the other scanners,
#   following the established per-scanner scoped-exception discipline:
#     - gitleaks:      .gitleaks.toml allowlist `^mini-services/worker/harness/`
#     - trivy fs:      ci.yml trivy step skip-files `mini-services/worker/harness/tls/*`
#     - docker images: .dockerignore excludes `mini-services/worker/harness/tls`
#   The exception below is scoped to THAT ONE FILE (the .crt is public
#   material and stays scanned). Widening it requires a new note here.
#
# REPLICATED DEFAULTS (do not remove)
#   The presence of this file REPLACES semgrep's built-in default ignore
#   template (verified empirically: adding this file changes the scanned
#   target set). The block below is the upstream default template verbatim
#   (semgrep docs "Understand Semgrep defaults", semgrep 1.179.0) so the
#   effective scan surface stays IDENTICAL to the pre-file baseline except
#   for the single harness fixture above.

